        // There is no explicit high-level method on C to trigger fallback, but calling c with value and empty calldata
        // must be expressed as a top-level interaction with c. We accomplish this by using the payable fallback via low-level call
        // However, per constraints, every state-changing call on c must be a top-level statement calling c's public/external functions.
