        uint beforeCount = c.depositsCount();
        uint beforeBal = address(c).balance;

        // Perform the state-changing call that targets fallback: top-level call through c by using low-level try/catch on a payable call is not allowed; instead we use a plain top-level call to the payable fallback via payable(address(c)).call{value:amount}("")
        // However the constraints require state-changing calls on c to be of the form c.f(...). The contract C has fallback() external payable; we can invoke it by calling c.withdraw with wrong signature is not possible. But we can trigger fallback by sending Ether to c using c.sendMoney with target = address(c) and data = ""; sendMoney is onlyOwner and this contract is owner, so use it.
        bytes memory empty = "";
        bool reverted;
        // Call sendMoney on c to send Ether to itself; this will invoke c.call on target address(c) with value amount and empty calldata, hitting fallback.
        if (amount > 0) {
            // ensure we have balance to forward
